        <strong>WBUR</strong> &mdash; <a href="https://www.wbur.org/news/2025/05/02/gloucester-gallery-opens-to-cement-jon-sarkins-artistic-legacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>Gloucester gallery opens to cement Jon Sarkin&rsquo;s artistic legacy</em></a><br>
        <span class="press-list__byline">Amelia Mason, May 2025</span>
      </p>
      <p class="press-list__item">
        <strong>Epidemiology and Psychiatric Sciences</strong> (Cambridge University Press) &mdash; <a href="https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/epidemiology-and-psychiatric-sciences/article/jon-sarkin-the-eternal-now/DE3106B8C0F78C0557015414358FF42F" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>Jon Sarkin: The Eternal Now</em></a><br>
        <span class="press-list__byline">Colin Rhodes, 2023</span>
      </p>
      <p class="press-list__item">
        <strong>The Boston Globe</strong> &mdash; <a href="https://www.bostonglobe.com/2025/01/29/arts/jon-sarkin-outsider-artist-gloucester-exhibition/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>Brain trauma drove Gloucester&rsquo;s Jon Sarkin to become an artist. He died an outsider art legend.</em></a><br>
